Q30. How do you handle multiple requests when updating inventory?
Scenario:

An online shop has only one item remaining.

Two users click Buy simultaneously.

Solution: Atomic database update.
UPDATE Product
SET stock = stock - 1
WHERE id = 101
AND stock > 0;


Then check the number of affected rows:
- 1 row updated: Inventory reserved.
- 0 rows updated: Out of stock.
This prevents the stock from becoming negative.

